      "id": "07f28c93-0e5b-4113-b3aa-eec4488f70e1",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Why is Java Platform Independent?\r\n\r\nJava follows the principle:\r\n\r\nWrite Once, Run Anywhere (WORA)\r\n\r\nJava source code is compiled into bytecode instead of directly into machine code.\r\n\r\nThe bytecode is executed by the JVM available on the target operating system.\r\n\r\nTherefore:\r\n\r\n```\r\nSame Java Bytecode\r\n       ↓\r\n ┌─────┼─────┐\r\n ↓     ↓     ↓\r\nWindows Linux macOS\r\n JVM    JVM    JVM",
